                <pb facs="1170" n="1158" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg1158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.00N/53: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-07T19:00:00-03:00">June 7, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>254. Aranha tells me that in accord with the Uruguayan Government, Brazilian
                    troops are being sent in the direction of the Uruguayan <pb facs="1171" n="1159"
                        xml:id="pg1159"/> frontier and a million rounds of ammunition are being
                    turned over to the Uruguayan Government, having in mind the possibility of a
                    Nazi inspired movement in Uruguay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
